{
  "tema": 6601,
  "slug": "cuyo-cuya",
  "titulo": "Cuyo, cuya, cuyos, cuyas = whose",
  "subtitulo": "Roberto, cuyo hijo va a la escuela de mi hija...",
  "foto": "t08.jpg",
  "regla": "Cuyo means whose and agrees in gender and number with the thing possessed, not with the owner: Marta, cuya jefa..., Roberto, cuyos hijos... It's formal; in speech people rephrase with que + su or de quien.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "owner",
            ", cuyo / cuya / cuyos / cuyas",
            "+ thing possessed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Agrees with **what follows**, like a possessive: **la escritora, cuyo libro... / el escritor, cuyas novelas...**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Can follow a preposition: **la casa en cuyas recámaras dormimos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Formal, mostly written. In speech: **Marta, que su jefa es mi jefa...** (colloquial) or **un amigo del que seguiste los consejos**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Never for questions: _Whose is this?_ = **¿De quién es esto?**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **cuyo** looks forward, like **su**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tabla",
      "titulo": "Forms",
